  "body": "## What changed\n\n- 3D Deburr has a new setting, `Unreachable edges`. Its values are `Skip with note` (the default) and `Refuse`.\n- `finishing3d::UnreachableEdges` is a new field of `DeburrParams` and of `OpParams::Deburr` (`unreachable`).\n- With `Skip with note`, the ride leaves each edge that is steeper than the flank of the cone. The note gives the count. This is the behaviour of each earlier Deburr.\n- With `Refuse`, the generator refuses the operation when one edge in the window is out of reach. The message gives the count, names the setting, and names `Skip with note` as the solution. No path is made.\n- The project file has the key `\"unreachable\": \"skip_with_note\" | \"refuse\"` in the `deburr` params. An earlier file without the key reads as `skip_with_note`. There is no `PROJECT_VERSION` step.\n- The parameter digest writes one byte for `Refuse` only. The stamp of each earlier Deburr does not change.\n- The Deburr page shows the combo `Unreachable edges` on the Geometry tab.\n- MCP needs no new tool. `add_operation` and `edit_operation` take `unreachable` in the params patch. `get_job` and `list_operation_types` show the field.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe kernel always skipped a steep edge with a note. The user had no setting to make this a refusal.\n\n## Tests\n\nNew pins in `crates/motion/tests/deburr_unreachable.rs`:\n\n- `skip_with_note_is_the_default_and_names_the_skipped_count`\n- `refuse_stops_the_ride_by_name_when_an_edge_is_out_of_reach`\n- `refuse_passes_when_every_candidate_edge_is_in_reach`\n- `refuse_does_not_count_an_edge_the_window_leaves_out`\n- `refuse_names_reach_before_empty_when_every_candidate_is_out_of_reach`\n\nNew pins in `crates/app/tests/deburr_unreachable.rs`:\n\n- `skip_with_note_generates_and_names_the_skipped_edges`\n- `refuse_refuses_the_operation_by_name_and_leaves_no_path`\n- `a_policy_edit_makes_the_generated_path_stale_and_undo_restores_it`\n- `a_policy_changed_outside_the_edit_command_makes_the_cached_path_stale`\n- `the_policy_round_trips_in_the_project_file`\n- `mcp_selects_the_two_modes_and_lists_the_field`\n\nRed before the fix: yes. The pins did not compile on `upstream/main` (`no UnreachableEdges in finishing3d`, `DeburrParams has no field named unreachable`).\n\nMutation results (each guard removed alone, then restored):\n\n| Mutation | Result |\n|---|---|\n| The `Refuse` guard in `deburr.rs` is off | red: 2 motion pins and `refuse_refuses_the_operation_by_name_and_leaves_no_path` |\n| `generate.rs` does not pass the policy to the kernel | red: `refuse_refuses_the_operation_by_name_and_leaves_no_path` |\n| The digest byte in `params/mill3d.rs` is off | red: `a_policy_changed_outside_the_edit_command_makes_the_cached_path_stale` |\n| `params_impl.rs` does not read the word from the file | red: `the_policy_round_trips_in_the_project_file`, `mcp_selects_the_two_modes_and_lists_the_field` |\n| All restored | green: 5 motion pins, 6 app pins |\n\nChanged tests (the change explains each one):\n\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests.rs`: the Deburr row of the tab table has the new label `Unreachable edges` on Geometry.\n- `crates/app/tests/operations.rs`: the seed test asserts the default policy.\n- Six test files get the new field in a hand-made `OpParams::Deburr` or `DeburrParams`.\n\nGate: `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` is green: 256 steps, 0 failed (motion, app and ui suites). `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings` is clean.\n\n## Geometry control screenshots\n\nThese images show the real Deburr Geometry page with synthetic data. A local CPU renderer draws the egui meshes and textures. The screenshot renderer has no graphics adapter.\n\nBefore: the new control and its hint are removed from the reviewed head for this capture.\n\n![Deburr Geometry before the new control](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/737640cf4cfab6db0780367bbcbc96b09214b228/2687/before.png)\n\nAfter: the reviewed head shows `Unreachable edges` with `Skip with note` selected.\n\n![Deburr Geometry with Unreachable edges](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/737640cf4cfab6db0780367bbcbc96b09214b228/2687/after.png)\n\nThe images are stored only on the fork's `pr-screenshots` branch at `737640cf4cfab6db0780367bbcbc96b09214b228`. The PR branch has no image or capture code.\n\nReview fix validation on `f3c4d3913e0d031dab9748ce58f64da944b177d8`:\n\n- `every_field_lives_on_exactly_one_section`: RED when the control is removed; GREEN after restoration.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: 256 steps, 0 failed.\n- Clippy for motion, app, and UI with `--all-targets -- -D warnings`: passed.\n- The source head is unchanged. This review fix adds only the requested PR evidence.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. `git diff --stat upstream/main -- \"*.nc\" \"*.cl\" \"*.cnc\"` is empty.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No UI test selects the combo with a pointer. The tab table test asserts that the row is on the Geometry tab.\n- The release lanes and the pixel snapshots did not run. The Deburr page has one more row, so a snapshot of that page can change at the cut.\n- The user documentation of the site does not have the new setting.\n- A Deburr that this build saves has one more key. I did not open such a file with an earlier build.\n\n## Overlaps\n\n- #2678, #2675, #2666, #2149 and #1713 change `crates/app/src/operation/generate.rs`, and #1713 also changes the params files. Each touches the same file, a different function or match arm. Whichever merges second refreshes.\n\nDecisions: `docs/decisions/1889-deburr-unreachable-policy.md`.\n\nEffort: high\n\nChangelog: 3D Deburr has an `Unreachable edges` setting: skip an edge that is steeper than the cone's flank with a note (default), or refuse the operation.\n\nFixes #1889\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
